{
  "abstract": "The arithmetic of one occupied genus-six component in the rational Diophantine septuple problem reduces to a three-dimensional Prym that is isomorphic to a quadratic twist of a plane-quartic Jacobian. Bitangent descent previously bounded its rational rank by three, subject to trivial two-torsion in an explicit S-class group. The remaining dimension arose from a possible local restriction kernel. We exclude that kernel by a local Picard obstruction. An exact multivariate Hensel certificate produces quadratic forms over the two-adic field whose weighted sum of squares is the quartic equation, yielding a morphism to an anisotropic conic. Pullback of the conic's geometric degree-one class gives the unique rational local two-torsion point with nonzero Brauer descent obstruction. Because the curve has a point over the quadratic splitting field, this torsion point cannot be a norm. A direct Kummer and inflation–restriction argument then proves injectivity on the twisted local Kummer subgroup. Combining this unconditional local theorem with the existing exact descent arithmetic gives rank and two-Selmer dimension both equal to two under the same explicit, still unproved S-class hypothesis. A standalone certificate replays the upper bound from text inputs in about91seconds; the new Hensel certificate also has an independent rational-arithmetic checker. The result supplies rank input for the existing Chabauty calculation but does not decide its two remaining entry candidates, prove the S-class hypothesis, or resolve the septuple problem.",
